{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Ham is the father of Canaan.</b> To teach that both of them were evil, and like the deed of the fathers the sons will do. And he mentioned Canaan and not Cush because he will curse Canaan. And this passage was written to make known that the Canaanites are accursed, and likewise their daughters from the days of Noah. And so Abraham said: \"You must not take a wife for my son from the daughters of the Canaanite\" (Genesis 24:3), and likewise Rebekah: \"from the daughters of these\" (Genesis 27:46). And perhaps a questioner will ask: What sin did the children of Heth commit, that he did not open his eyes? For the Hittite and the Amorite and the others are all children of Canaan; therefore Scripture says: \"to the land of Canaan\" (Joshua 22:32)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The verse citation יהושע כב לב does not correspond to any text about 'the land of Canaan' in the received book of Joshua; the reference is uncertain and may reflect a different verse enumeration or a textual corruption."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:00.676540435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}